Cholesky input-protocol correction:
  The first diagnostic harness accumulated the positive-semidefinite input in
  r,s,t order. That diagnostic was rejected because canonical PolyBench/C uses
  t,r,s order. scripts/correctness/polybench_cholesky_validation.c was changed
  to exactly match t,r,s, the binary was rebuilt on x86, and it was redeployed.
  The corrected run produced the same failure line shown above.

Disposition:
  cholesky=FAIL; do not time or publish as an accepted LARGE result
